of Czechoslovakia during World War II, settling in New York in 1941.", "early_education_description": null, "artlens_description": null, "description": "<em>Test Proof</em> is typical of Terry Haass\u2019s early work at the New York print workshop founded by Stanley William Hayter, Atelier 17. She combined three different print techniques to create a combination of hard edges and emerging and disappearing forms.", "external_resources": {"wikidata": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q117247720"], "internet_archive": []}, "citations": [], "url": "https://clevelandart.org/art/2022.258", "images": {}, "alternate_images": [], "creditline": "Gift of Pete and Margaret Dobbins in honor of Emily Peters", "image_credit": null, "sketchfab_id": null, "sketchfab_url": null, "gallery_donor_text": null, "athena_id": 534896, "creators": [{"id": 49159, "description": "Terry Haass (Czech, 1923\u20132016)", "extent": null, "qualifier": null, "role": "artist", "biography": null, "name_in_original_language": null, "birth_year": "1923", "death_year": "2016", "use_in_caption": true, "include_extent": false, "weight": 1}], "legal_status": "accessioned", "accession_date": "2022-12-05T05:00:00Z", "sortable_date": 1949, "date_added_to_oa": null, "date_text": "1949\u201350", "collapse_artists": false, "on_loan": false, "recently_acquired": false, "record_type": "object", "conservation_statement": null, "has_conservation_images": false, "cover_accession_number": null, "is_nazi_era_provenance": false, "impression": null, "alternate_titles": [], "is_highlight": false, "updated_at": "2026-05-01 06:54:25.577000"}]}